      "code_excerpt": "public final static String USERLEVELS_GETPHP = \"http://www.apo-games.de/apoElf/get_level.php\";\npublic final static String USERLEVELS_SAVEPHP = \"http://www.apo-games.de/apoElf/save_level.php\";",
      "entry_point": "Automatic background download at startup: ApoImpPanel.init -> loadUserlevels() spawns a Thread (ApoImpPanel.java:78-81, 204-212) -> ApoImpUserlevels.loadUserlevels() -> ApoImpUserlevelsLoad.load(). Upload path: editor Upload button -> ApoImpEditor.uploadString() -> ApoImpUserlevels.addLevel() -> ApoImpUserlevelsLoad.save()",
      "sink": "urlConn = url.openConnection(); ... printout.writeBytes(content); ... input = new DataInputStream(urlConn.getInputStream()) in ApoImpUserlevelsLoad.save (lines 123-143) and load (lines 164-210)",
      "data_path": "Startup thread calls ApoImpUserlevelsLoad.load(), which opens http://www.apo-games.de/apoElf/get_level.php, POSTs \"Get=\", then reads the response line-by-line into 11 parallel ArrayLists (level string + metadata). Every 11th line (i%11==0) is stored verbatim as a level string in this.levels, later copied into ApoImpLevel.editorLevels (ApoImpUserlevels.getAllLevelsSorted, line 28/48). Uploads POST \"level=<raw string>\" unencrypted.",
      "attack_scenario": "Attacker on the same LAN (or any DNS/network hijack of www.apo-games.de, no TLS so no warning possible) answers get_level.php with crafted rows whose numeric columns are digits but whose i%11==0 'level' lines are hostile payloads (see ApoImp-02). The payload is fetched automatically at game start; the victim just clicks the 'userlevels' menu button and the malformed level is parsed, crashing the game. Uploaded levels can equally be stripped/replaced in transit, poisoning the shared level pool.",
      "reachable": true,
